    "bbox": [
      139.15,
      293.71,
      451.2,
      360.98
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2: This clause inserts new section 122A in the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No. 15of 1979 and the legal effect of the amendment is to enable the officer in charge of a police stationto cause, a child of, or above twelve years of age and under fourteen, alleged to have committed anoffence, to be examined with the consent of the parent or guardian of such child, by a Governmentmedical officer or other expert in the relevant field, in order to assist the Magistrate to form hisopinion on the maturity of understanding of such child, to act in compliance with the provisions ofsection 76 of the Penal Code.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
